# UI Screen Documentation (definitive)

Authoritative rules for documenting **player-app** screens and screen-like surfaces (routes, full-screen hosts, modal dialogs, overlays). **Style, palette, pixel-art generation, and thematic conventions** are orthogonal — see `colonizethis-ui-design.mdc` and per-screen asset sections only when assets are layout inputs.

**SPEC location:** One spec per screen at `SPEC/ui/<kebab-name>.md`. **Registry:** [`SPEC/ui/screen-registry.md`](../../SPEC/ui/screen-registry.md). **Code IDs:** `app/lib/config/ui_screen_ids.dart`.

---

## Screen ID format (stable)

Every screen gets a **unique 8-character ID**, assigned once and **never changed**.

| Segment | Chars | Meaning |
|---------|-------|---------|
| Category | 1–3 | Uppercase flow code (see registry § Categories). Few major categories only. |
| Sub-flow | 4 | Single digit `0`–`9` within the category. |
| Screen | 5–8 | Four digits `0001`–`9999` within that sub-flow; allocate sequentially per sub-flow. |

**Variants:** Append one lowercase letter to the base ID: `MAP10001a`, `MAP10001b`. Variants share one spec file under **States and variants** unless layout/behavior diverge enough to warrant a separate spec (then new base ID).

**Examples:** `SHEL10001` (shell route host), `GAME10001` (game screen), `MAP20001` (province overlay), `DLG30001a` (dialog variant).

### Code binding

- Declare each base screen ID as a `static const String` on `UiScreenIds` in `app/lib/config/ui_screen_ids.dart`.
- The screen widget (or route host) must expose the ID for traceability, e.g. `static const screenId = UiScreenIds.gameScreen;` or `UiScreenIds.of(context)` where a mixin applies.
- Widgetbook folder names and spec headings use the human title; the **ID** is the cross-reference key in the registry and code reviews.
- Do not embed IDs only in comments; they must be const values grep-able from tests.

---

## When to write or update a spec

- **New** route, screen, dialog, or overlay in `app/lib/features/`, `app/lib/screens/`, or shell widgets mounted as a primary surface.
- **Changed** layout hierarchy, triggers, bus events, provider inputs, variants, or Widgetbook use cases.
- **New composite widget** used by multiple screens → add `SPEC/ui/components/<name>.md` first, then reference it from screen specs.

ctdev-only screens stay in `SPEC/program/ctdev-app.md`; this rule does not apply there.

---

## Spec document template

Use this section order. Keep each spec ≤1000 words; split component detail into `SPEC/ui/components/`.

```markdown
# <Human title>

**Screen ID:** `<CATEGORY><sub><####>` — stable; do not reassign.
**SPEC/ui** — <one-line purpose>. Implementation: `<relative/dart/path.dart>`.
**Widgetbook:** `<Folder name>` → `app/lib/widgetbook/...`

## Widget contract
| Name | Type | Required | Description |
...

## Trigger conditions
Exhaustive entry: routes (`Routes.*`), bus events (`OpenDialogEvent`, `NavigateToRouteEvent`, …),
parent screens, provider predicates. Link `SPEC/program/app-ui-wiring.md` / `app-event-bus.md`.

## Layout / wireframe
ASCII wireframe with hierarchy indentation. List every visible control region.
Name **Ct-*** catalog widgets and layout primitives (`Stack`, `Positioned`, …).
Reference `SPEC/ui/components/<x>.md` for composite widgets instead of redefining them.

## Behavior
### Incoming (what shows this UI)
| Source | Condition | Result |
...

### User actions → outcomes
| Control / gesture | When enabled | Emits / calls | Side effects |
...
Bus emissions must name **event types and payload fields**. Local `Navigator` only where
`app-ui-wiring.md` allows. No "etc." — list every interactive control.

## States and variants
| ID | Variant | Trigger | Render difference |
...
Base ID row required; variant suffix letter when applicable.

## Components
Bullet list: widget class, spec link, role in hierarchy.

## Widgetbook
Folder name, catalog part file, each **use case name** and what it proves
(providers/overrides, variant ID). At least one mobile use case when layout differs
(`SPEC/ui/mobile-adaptation.md`).

## Acceptance criteria
Given–When–Then per `colonizethis-acceptance-criteria.mdc`; map to tests.
```

---

## Layout rules

- Wireframe must be sufficient to recreate structure in Flutter/Flame without guessing parent/child relationships.
- Use **region names** (e.g. `title_region`, `buttons_region`) when multiple bands exist.
- Positions: edge anchors (`top:16`, `left:16`), flex/scroll behavior, max widths, z-order for stacks.
- **Catalog-first:** [`pixel-art-ui-catalog.md`](../../SPEC/ui/pixel-art-ui-catalog.md), existing `SPEC/ui/components/`, and `app/widget_catalog.json` before inventing widgets.
- **New composites:** Author `SPEC/ui/components/<kebab-name>.md` (props, sub-layout, states) and reference by link from screen specs.

---

## Behavior rules (exhaustive)

- **Triggers:** Every path that mounts the screen (initial route, bus handler, parent callback, push from another screen).
- **Emissions:** Every tap/gesture/submit/back that emits `AppEventBus` events or calls services — with event class and key fields.
- **Gating:** Document disable conditions (`turnResolutionBlockingProvider`, empty lists, victory set, …) per control.
- **Navigation:** No cross-screen `Navigator` chains unless spec-authorised in `app-ui-wiring.md`; prefer bus events.
- **Flame vs Flutter:** Game canvas behavior stays in game/GDD specs; screen spec only describes host chrome and handoff.

---

## Registry maintenance

When assigning an ID:

1. Pick category + sub-flow from [`screen-registry.md`](../../SPEC/ui/screen-registry.md).
2. Take next free `####` in that sub-flow.
3. Add a row: ID, title, spec path, Dart path, Widgetbook folder, status (`draft` | `active`).
4. Add `UiScreenIds` constant and widget `screenId` binding in the same change.

---

## Widgetbook linkage

- Every **active** screen spec lists Widgetbook folder + use cases matching `app/lib/widgetbook/catalog*.dart`.
- Use case names should align with **States and variants** (e.g. "Victory", "No saves", "Default (mobile)").
- New/changed screens require catalog registration in the same PR as the spec update.

